From 5e1649111f96a3f0fde4c6454ec019f4c172f099 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 19:29:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 5: wire entries-only paper order submission (v0.5.3.26)

Adds the missing piece that turns .23's execution specifications into
actual (or validate-only) Alpaca paper orders, and wires the whole
entries tail into the runtime supervisor. Scope and defaults confirmed
with Martin before building:

- ENTRIES ONLY. No closing/exit order path -- .24's (Phase 3) EXIT
  decisions are not wired to anything here. That stays out of scope
  until asked for.
- .23's VALIDATED_LONG_ENTRY_REGIME_LABELS / VALIDATED_SHORT_ENTRY_
  REGIME_LABELS allowlists are left untouched (still empty) -- Martin
  explicitly deferred that decision, so every symbol still fails closed
  with NO_VALIDATED_EXECUTION_DIRECTION for now. This module only
  relays whatever .23 already decided; it can't grant a direction .23
  didn't already validate.
- OFF BY DEFAULT. Real submission needs --submit-paper on the new
  aura_v05326_paper_order_submission.py glue AND .22's own independent
  AURA_ALPACA_PAPER_ORDERS_ENABLED=true -- two explicit switches,
  neither sufficient alone. Without --submit-paper, every ready symbol
  is still built and still sent through .22, but only ever reaches
  VALIDATED_NO_SUBMISSION, and needs no Alpaca credentials for that path.

- aura_v05326_paper_order_submission.py: the actual glue. .23 produces
  one multi-symbol execution_specification.json; .22 accepts exactly one
  spec per invocation. This module extracts every EXECUTION_SPEC_READY
  symbol and calls .22 (unmodified, as a subprocess) once per symbol,
  never touching BLOCKED symbols, never inventing a result when the
  adapter process itself fails (ADAPTER_FAILED, with stderr attached).
  11 new tests, all against the real .22 script in its validate-only
  mode (no credentials needed/used).

- aura_v05321_alpaca_paper_runtime.py: additive wiring only -- the
  existing .12-.19 cycle is untouched. Appends .25 (position sizing) ->
  .23 (execution spec) -> .26 (this module) after .19 every cycle, and
  adds a new --submit-paper flag (default off) forwarded only to .26.
  Docstring updated to describe the new conditional capability honestly
  rather than leave the old "never places an order" claim stale.
  6 new static contract checks added to the existing runtime validator
  (all passing); full suite at 163/163 (excluding the 2 pre-existing
  tests that require live Alpaca credentials, unrelated to this change).

